# Re-applied 2026-07-30: rolls the current backend image to 100% traffic. That
# image carries the CORRECTED SourceColumn merge key — a pattern merge on the
# table node, which is both tenant-scoped and stable across re-profiles. The
# previous key, (tablePgId, columnName), fixed the cross-tenant collision but
# would have accumulated duplicate columns on every Analyse, because the profiler
# rebuilds its Postgres rows so source_tables.id changes each run.
#
# This must be live BEFORE the next sync/Analyse, or the duplicates start.
#
# Promote vehicle on purpose: this workflow waits for the NEW revision to reach
# Provisioned and fails loudly otherwise. deploy.yml never waits at all, and
# promote.yml shifts to latestReadyRevisionName, which silently promotes the
# PREVIOUS revision if the new one failed to boot. The mode itself is unchanged.
